From: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ask2(T-M6-2 B1): add SRC_MAC/ETHERTYPE to the bridge FDB match key struct

Completes struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key's bridge FDB match-key surface:
B0 (patch 0202) added FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_DST + dst_mac[6] and
explicitly left the full byte layout as an "open silicon question."
This adds FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_SRC + src_mac[6] and
FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_ETHERTYPE + ethertype_be, completing the vendor
15-byte PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE composite B1's own plan section names.

Resolves that open question with a board reading, not a guess: live
.106 KeyGen scheme 11 (EKFC 0xe4000000 = PORT_ID|MACDST|MACSRC|ETYPE,
the vendor's real L2/bridge classification scheme -- 1,225,734 live
packets, by far the highest-traffic scheme observed) has a
group-table row keysize field of 15, matching PORT_ID(1)+DA(6)+
SA(6)+ETYPE(2) exactly. Captured via bin/fman-full-capture.py
--follow-rccb during this session's T-M6-T3 work; reused here rather
than re-reading the board.

Purely additive, same as B0: no existing field moves, no existing
packer touched, no caller sets the new presence bits, so every
existing CC key stays byte-identical. Paired with a new
cc_pack_key_l2() in fman_pcd_cc.c (separate commit/patch) that
targets these fields.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GooC2zFmzRBYLikPbwekuH
---
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -514,1 +514,10 @@
 #define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_DST	BIT(7)
+/* T-M6-2 B1: source MAC + EtherType, completing the vendor 15-byte
+ * PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE bridge FDB match key. Board-confirmed 2026-09-14
+ * (live .106 KeyGen scheme 11 group-table row, keysize field = 15,
+ * matching PORT_ID(1)+DA(6)+SA(6)+ETYPE(2) exactly -- resolves the "open
+ * silicon question" B0's comment above flagged). Presence bits + byte
+ * slots only, same as B0's MAC_DST: no packer emits these yet.
+ */
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_SRC	BIT(8)
+#define FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_ETHERTYPE	BIT(9)
@@ -543,3 +554,10 @@
 * @dst_mac:      L2 destination MAC (6 bytes, network order).  Valid only
 *                when FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_DST is set.  T-M6-2 bridge FDB
 *                match key; dormant until a bridge key packer exists (B1).
+ * @src_mac:      L2 source MAC (6 bytes, network order).  Valid only when
+ *                FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_SRC is set.  T-M6-2 bridge FDB match
+ *                key, completes the PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE composite with
+ *                @dst_mac and @ethertype_be.
+ * @ethertype_be: EtherType (2 bytes, BE).  Valid only when
+ *                FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_ETHERTYPE is set.  T-M6-2 bridge FDB
+ *                match key.
@@ -571,1 +585,3 @@
 	u8  dst_mac[6];
+	u8  src_mac[6];
+	u16 ethertype_be;
